  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Gate" id="214c-d5be-32e8-9271" hidden="false">
      <description>If your Army contains Gates, any of your Squads may start the game in Holding. Gates are always Transports but are not taken with any Units aboard. Gates do not count against your number of allowed Groups. For Direct Deployment, each Gate is treated as a Group. A Gate is never part of another Group, but any number of them which have not yet been activated that Round may be activated together with any non-Gate Group. They then complete that activation as if they were a Group. Gates can only be activated this way except during in the Orphaned Transport Activations step of the Activation Phase, where any un-activated Gates must activate together. Squads in Holding may Disembark from ANY Gate/s providing their Transport Symbols match. Squads which Embark into Gates are placed into Holding. Any Objects they are carrying are passed to the Gate, even if it&apos;s an Aircraft. Squads may Embark or Disembark into or from a Gate during their own Activation, even if the Gate is not a part of that Activation. All other Embarking/Disembarking rules and restrictions still apply. Additionally, Gates may not Embark/Disembark more than their Symbol indicates per Round, but they may do both. For example, a Gate with 6 could Embark 6, then Disembark 6. Units in Holding at the end of the game only count as destroyed if you have no Units which could return them to the Table if there were another Round.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Aux Gate" id="58fc-735e-cb69-eadf" hidden="false">
      <description>These are always Auxiliary Transports. They use the same rules as Gates except they are taken as non-Gate Squads and must be activated normally—they cannot be activated together with another non-Gate Group. Other Squads can still Embark/Disembark from them outside of that Aux Gate&apos;s activation. Aux Gates cannot attack in the same round as Embarking/Disembarking. Command Cards which target Gates cannot target these.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Microgate" id="62ea-d6c5-e865-be25" hidden="false">
      <description>This Unit, and Units in coherency with it, gain Regenerate 2. At the beginning of this Unit&apos;s activation, if all Units in its Squad are in coherency, you may place its Squad into Holding—this is an Embark operation. Any Objects this Squad is carrying must be dropped or passed to another Unit first.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Subservient" id="8a1e-a4e5-afbd-9212" hidden="false">
      <description>Subservient Units gain +2B and +2OF when occupying a Zone containing a friendly Unit without Subservient. Subservient Units in a Squad which also contains Units without Subservient gain any special rules those Units have. Commanders cannot be assigned to Subservient Units.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warsuit" id="65f0-9db9-b27d-69da" hidden="false">
      <description>Small Arms Weapons and Weapons of E2 or lower which target this Infantry Unit must use their 2nd range value.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Aircharge" id="f714-af47-2b6f-47ca" hidden="false">
      <description>This Weapon uses the same rules as an AA-R Weapon. Additionally, a Unit may only be targeted by a Weapon with this rule once during its activation.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Grav" id="a8df-8f0e-e908-ab36" hidden="false">
      <description>When targeting Vehicles, add the target&apos;s initial DP to this Weapon&apos;s E. For Vehicles of A4 or higher add 1 more, or for Vehicles of A7 or higher add 2 more. For Vehicles with Large, it gains +1 Devastator. This Weapon ignores Resilient on Vehicles. This Weapon always damages Zones on a 3+ and has a Demo value equal to its E.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Particle" id="33e9-1e21-b57e-867e" hidden="false">
      <description>This Weapon ignores Passive Countermeasures and Resilient.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Skimcharger" id="9a63-f99c-6a08-3447" hidden="false">
      <description>If a friendly Squad with Skimmer receives at least as many hits from Weapons with Skimcharger during a single Activation as it has Units, place a Skimcharged Status Token on its Squad. Skimcharged Squads gain Flat Out 5&quot;, +5&quot; MA on their Weapons, and may benefit from Flat Out even if they Attack (but not if they Embark or Disembark).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
